    ],
    "description": "Title:\nHemingray Glass Insulator Pale Yellow Stepped Industrial Collector Piece\nBrand:\nHemingray\nCondition:\nUsed\nCondition Description:\nUsed - surface cloudiness, residue, minor marks\nCategory:\nCollectibles & Art\nType:\nElectrical Insulator\nFeatures:\nStepped design, Drip points, Aged surfaces\nUnit Quantity:\n1\nUnit Type:\nUnit\nDescription:\nAdd a distinct piece of industrial history to your collection with this vintage Hemingray glass transformer cap insulator. Crafted from a single mold of pale yellow-tinted transparent glass, this insulator features a classic stepped upper section, broad flared skirt, and projecting circular ridges. The Hemingray name is embossed on the side, a hallmark recognized by collectors of electrical equipment and glassware alike. Rounded drip points circle the bottom rim, and the underside reveals a hollow design with a central mounting recess. Visible surface cloudiness, light residue, scattered marks, and small production irregularities reflect the cap's age and history of use, enhancing its character as a display piece. No model number or date is confirmed from photos. Intended for display or collectible purposes, suitability for active electrical service is unverified. This listing includes a single glass insulatorperfect for glass insulator enthusiasts, those passionate about electrical history, or anyone seeking an industrial Chic decor accent",
